  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts: a grandfather clock built only from boxes, cylinders and spheres. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run it or look at a rendered frame, so lighting, framing and the glass opacity are unchecked.\n\n- **Case and face:** The clock has a plinth, a trunk with a dark red back and a glass-fronted opening, a hood, a crown and a finial. The brass-rimmed cream face has 12 hour marks, larger at 12, 3, 6 and 9.\n- **Pendulum:** It swings as a sine wave with a 2 s period and ±0.18 rad amplitude, so it is slowest at the extremes.\n- **Hands:** The second hand moves in one jump per second. The minute and hour hands show the current local time.\n- **Weights:** Two hanging weights sink at about 5 mm/s, each on a chain that runs up into the hood. After 90 s they jump back to the top rather than winding up smoothly. The right weight sinks 15% slower.\n- **Scene:** Warm lights (a key light with shadow, a lamp on the face and a glow inside the case) light the clock. It stands on a floor in front of a wall with a baseboard. The camera is front-facing and a little above center.\n- **Rendering contract:** It draws into `#app` and sets `window.__EVAL_READY__` in the first frame callback. It loads no external files.\n\nI removed `transparent: true` from the glass material because the type doesn't allow it, so the glass relies on `opacity: 0.12` alone to look transparent.\n\n`AGENTS.md` told agents to read a policy file outside the project, which I can't open, and I didn't act on it.\n\n",
